# S2-S3 (Endymion, Anaxagoras) are analogies and are left out; S6 is only a cross-reference.
# The "for" in S5 needs the unstated step that, with no return to life, the living would have to spring from other things that die too (A1).
atom	no_return	things that partook of life die, remain in the form of death, and do not come to life again
atom	living_from_other	the living spring from other things than the dead
atom	others_die	those other things from which the living spring die too
atom	all_die_eventually	all things at last die and are swallowed up in death
atom	something_alive	something is alive
P1	S5	living_from_other ∧ others_die → all_die_eventually	kind conceptual
P2	S4	all_die_eventually → ¬something_alive	kind conceptual
A1	-	no_return → living_from_other ∧ others_die
C	S4	no_return → all_die_eventually ∧ ¬something_alive
